    "body": "## What's the issue?\r\n\r\nIf AMP is used for tracking and it is legally required to have opted in to tracking or for the user to at have least seen the cookie dialog the iframe can not contain custom tracking, unless a custom dialog is shown, since the iframe is unaware of the tracking state of the AMP document. \r\n\r\nThe iframe also has to load additional tracking scripts which might impact the page/iframe performance. The duplicate implementation of tracking and unnecessary load of additional scripts might easily be avoided if the iframe could postMessage to the AMP page, where AMP-analytics could then execute a predefined trigger to handle the calls.    \r\n\r\n## How do we reproduce the issue?\r\n\r\n1. build simple amp page with amp-analytics trigger predefined\r\n2. include amp-iframe in page\r\n3. build simple iframe content page with post message implementation to trigger tracking event on link/button click\r\n4. click button/link inside iframe\r\n5. fire tracking request on AMP page prior to link navigation\r\n\r\n## What browsers are affected?\r\n\r\nAll browsers for new feature.\r\n\r\n## Which AMP version is affected?\r\n\r\nUpcoming if implemented.",
